|passage={{...}} found out a discarded sex mini-game in the code, and made it available again in the modified PC version of the game that they nicknamed “Hot Coffee.” This '''hack''' of the game created a controversy, since the inclusion of sexual content would change its age rating, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|{{w|Massachusetts Institute of Technology}}}} A [[practical joke]] that showcases cleverness and creativity.
# {{lb|en|slang|military}} [[time check|Time check]], as for example upon synchronization of wristwatches.
#: <small>Related terms:</small> {{w|hack watch}}
# {{lb|en|[[ice hockey]]}} The act of striking an opponent with one's [[hockey stick]], typically on the leg but occasionally and more seriously on the back, arm, head, etc.
#: {{ux|en|Zersky is still down after that nasty '''hack''' by Lenner.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} A [[swing]] of the [[bat]] at a pitched ball by the [[batter]], particularly a choppy, ungraceful one that misses the ball such as at a [[fastball]].
#: {{ux|en|And Melnick goes down with one last hack at an O'Malley fastball.}}
# A [[kick]] on the [[shin]]s in [[football]] of any type.
#: {{ux|en|Wales are awarded a free kick after a minor '''hack''' by Järvinen on Llewellyn.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1857|author=Thomas Hughes|title=Tom Brown's School Days
|passage=“Ain't there just fine scrummages then! and the three trees you see there which come out into the play, that's a tremendous place when the ball hangs there, for you get thrown against the trees, and that's worse than any '''hack'''.”}}
