|passage=Henebry's planes returned to Japan to reload, and early in the morning brought almost 3,000 more troopers to Korea {{...}} Before sunrise next day, all troops in the maneuver had been picked up again and airlifted in “Henebry '''Hacks'''” back to Japan.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1967|title=Christian Advocate|volume=47|page=292
|passage={{...}} so that he had to make the 300-mile journey in a “'''hack'''” plane which had spluttering engines, which did not conduce to an easy mind nor to a comfortable journey; {{...}}}}

